From 28ae37fb453e6b2479047485bab9608560503fcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gilli <272772515+amd-cgilli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:53:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf] [AMD] QSA: fused FlyDSL sparse decode on gfx950

Serve Qwen sparse attention decode/verify on gfx950 with a FlyDSL kernel that
reads the selected KV straight from the pool through req_to_token (no gather
pass, no packed scratch) and splits each row's top-k list across CTAs, with a
small FlyDSL reduce over the splits. It is tried after the trtllm branch and
before the Triton gather + sparse_gqa_packed_decode_triton fallback.

SGLANG_ENABLE_QSA_FLYDSL_DECODE (default on) is the kill switch; other GPUs
and unsupported operands keep the Triton path.

Original kernel by Nikolai Protasov.
